 function, set to =CF=95(x) =3D elu(x)+1.</p><p><span>This approximation is=
 efficient because it avoids explicitly computing the n=C3=97n attention ma=
trix QK</span><sup>T</sup><span>.</span></p><p><span>I don=E2=80=99t want t=
o dwell too long on these older attempts. But the bottom line was that they=
 reduced both time and memory complexity from O(n</span><sup>2</sup><span>)=
 to O(n) to make attention much more efficient for long sequences.</span></=
p><p>However, they never really gained traction as they degraded the model =
accuracy, and I have never really seen one of these variants applied in an =
open-weight state-of-the-art LLM.</p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post"><stro=
