 improving efficiency and making models faster or more scalable. And these =
approaches usually come at a slightly degraded modeling performance.</p><p>=
Now, the topic in this section takes a different angle and focuses on impro=
ving modeling performance (not efficiency). This improved performance is ac=
hieved by teaching the models an =E2=80=9Cunderstanding of the world.=E2=80=
=9D</p><p><span>World models have traditionally been developed independentl=
y of language modeling, but the recent </span><a href=3D"https://www.arxiv.=
org/abs/2510.02387">Code World Models</a><span> paper in September 2025 has=
 made them directly relevant in this context for the first time.</span></p>=
<p>Ideally, similar to the other topics of this article, world models are a=
